<title>USA: U.S. M-2 money supply up $17.3 bln in Jan 6 week.</title>
<headline>U.S. M-2 money supply up $17.3 bln in Jan 6 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. M-2 money supply rose $17.3 billion in the January 6 week to $3,841.7 billion, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>The broader M-3 measure rose $10.5 billion to $4,909.5 billion. M-1 fell $3.9 billion to $1,075.0 billion, the Fed said.</p>
<p>The Fed said the four-week moving average of M-2 was $3,830.1 billion versus $3,825.3 billion in the previous week.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
